he new records have E not having Ivory 4. \n\nSo after the change, the new records would have E without Ivory 4. Then, applying Rule 10, E gets Lilac 5, then Copper 6, then Rule 12 says not Indigo 10. Therefore, the conclusion would be that Indigo 10 is contradicted. So the proposed target is C. \n\nBut the question is whether the candidate reasoning is sufficient to apply the change and make C the answer. The reasoning for the change is based on EDIT107, which requires that the origin check passed for Record R. The observed records say that Record R (Ivory 4) passed the origin check, and the candidate justification steps are valid. So the change is applied. Then, with the new records, the answer becomes C. Therefore, the candidate reasoning is sufficient. So the answer should be B (sufficient).\n</think>\n\n{\"judgment\":\"B\"}",
